spec:
  grid: 10-17 rows x 10-17 cols, always square [observed]
  colors: exactly 3 distinct colors — left_color, middle_color, right_color
  row_structure: |
    Every row = [left_color x L] [middle_color x M] [right_color x R]
    where L >= 0, M >= 1, R >= 0, L + M + R = width.
    At least one row has L >= 1 and at least one has R >= 1 (so all 3 colors appear).
  middle_color: uniquely the most common color overall (40-60% of cells)
  run_widths: vary per row; range 3 to 0.7*width; at least 3 distinct widths across rows
  left_prefix: 0-6 cells; varies across rows with >= 3 distinct values
  right_suffix: 0-8 cells; varies across rows
  anchor_constraint: |
    Let anchor_end = min right-edge of middle runs across all rows.
    Rows at anchor_end have L >= 1 (never start at col 0).
    The widest left_color prefix stops at or just before anchor_end:
    0 <= anchor_end - max(L) <= 2.
    At least 1 non-anchor row must have a run wider than anchor_end+1 (causes clamp to col 0).
  transform: |
    Shift each row's middle run left so its right edge aligns to anchor_end
    (clamped at col 0 if run too wide). Displaced left-prefix pixels fill
    between run end and right suffix. Right suffix preserved. Color counts unchanged.

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    - Pick grid size N x N (10-17). Pick 3 distinct colors for left, middle, right.
    - Choose anchor_end in range [floor(0.3*N), floor(0.6*N)].
    - For each row, pick run_width M in [3, floor(0.7*N)].
    - Compute output start = max(0, anchor_end - M + 1), output end = start + M - 1.
    - Pick right_suffix R for each row in [0, N - output_end - 1], ensuring at least one R >= 1.
    - Fill output row = [left x (N-M-R - offset)] [middle x M] [left x offset] [right x R], where offset = max(0, output_end - anchor_end) for rows whose run extends past anchor_end.
    - Derive input by sliding each run right by a random shift S >= 0, moving S left-prefix cells from before the run to after it. S = 0 for anchor rows (those already at anchor_end). Ensure at least one row has L_input = 0 if desired.
    - Validate: middle is most common color; all 3 colors present; >=3 distinct run widths; max input left_prefix is in [anchor_end-2, anchor_end]; at least one run wider than anchor_end+1.
